Modifications made when vendoring: the max-pool and stage strides were changed
to (1, 2, 2) so that an 8-frame clip keeps its temporal extent through the
trunk; the classifier head was dropped and forward() now returns the layer4
feature map; and a loader was added for upstream checkpoint payloads.


B.2  abnet/models/gaitgl.py — architecture attribution

This file implements the GaitGL architecture of

    B. Lin, S. Zhang, X. Yu. "Gait Recognition via Effective Global-Local
    Feature Representation and Local Temporal Aggregation." ICCV 2021.

It was written for this repository, following the paper together with the
official release at https://github.com/bb12346/GaitGL (model/network/vgg_c3d.py,
class C3D_VGG) and cross-checked against the OpenGait reference implementation
at https://github.com/ShiqiYu/OpenGait (Apache License 2.0). It additionally
adds an identity classification head, which upstream does not provide and which
the knowledge-distillation objective requires.

Note on upstream terms: the bb12346/GaitGL repository publishes no license
file, so it grants no explicit permissions. Nothing in this repository should
be read as a license to that upstream code. If you need rights to the original
release, seek them from its authors. The OpenGait implementation consulted
during cross-checking is Apache License 2.0.


B.3  Runtime-downloaded models (not distributed here)

The following are fetched at runtime by preprocessing tools and are governed by
their own terms. No weights are distributed with this repository.

    Mask2Former — tools/extract_silhouettes.py
        Used through HuggingFace Transformers (Apache License 2.0) with Meta's
        released COCO checkpoints, or optionally through the official
        implementation at https://github.com/facebookresearch/Mask2Former
        (MIT License, Copyright (c) Meta Platforms, Inc.).

    OpenCV SSD ResNet-10 face detector — tools/blur_faces.py
        Fetched from https://github.com/opencv and
        https://github.com/opencv/opencv_3rdparty, Apache License 2.0.

    ResNet3D-50 Kinetics weights — abnet/models/resnet3d.py
        Fetched by the user from 3D-ResNets-PyTorch (MIT License).


